  "body": "## What changed\n\nTier 1 of the #578 split (tiers and drops kept in `docs/decisions/578-units-in-errors.md`): transient strings - the ones that quote the numbers the user is already reading on screen - format at print time through `app::units::of(world)` and the pure `geometry::units` formatters. Millimeter strings stay byte-identical (the `len`/`feed`/`area` law: inches ride the mm precision plus extra decimals); only inch documents hear anything new.\n\n- `geometry::units`: new `vol` formatter (inches get `mm_prec + 3`, mirroring `area`) and `Unit::vol_suffix`'s superscript spellings \"mm³\"/\"in³\" (matching `area_suffix`; a plain \"mm3\" would have changed the mm strings). Re-exported by `app::units`.\n- The posting gate's gouge clause (`posting_sim::sim_clause`): worst depth and its location lens - `worst 0.1969 in at (-0.0246, -0.0738, z 0.1969)`.\n- `commands/set_stock` refusal: `stock dimensions exceed 1000000 mm` - the shape changes from the old `{:e}`'s \"1e6 mm\" (see the correction comment on #578; the issue body's \"2000 mm\" misquoted it).\n- `commands/cutting_data` \"already runs the suggestion\": spindle and feed through `feed`/`feed_suffix`.\n- UI status strings: the applied-suggestion note, the tool-body tip offset, the feeds page's fz note, and the setup stock page's box range and volume (the only volume sentence in the UI).\n- `ui::actions::deviate_readout` takes a `Unit` parameter, mirroring its sibling `sim_readout(&sc, t, Unit)`; both callers pass the world lens.\n\nHeld back, with reasons in the decision file: persisted notes (they freeze the unit into the `.camproj`; they want `Warning`-shaped structured notes - its own issue), machine-limit strings (those speak the machine's numbers; the inch-`.mch` unit-never-converted bug is noted on the issue, not fixed here), and the generator/pure-crate refusals (no world or unit in scope below the app).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `blind_floor::the_gouge_clause_speaks_the_document_s_units` - the same gouging world told in inches (\"... in at (...)\", no \"mm\" anywhere); flip the lens back to mm and the sentence is unchanged.\n- `egui_app::tests::deviate_readout_rides_the_units_lens` - REST and GOUGE sentences pinned in inches; the mm pins next to them untouched.\n\n## Quick gate, green at 7775c1ff\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --no-run` clean, zero warnings. Then: `geometry --lib` 39, `app --lib` 101, `ui --lib` 378 (5 ignored), and the touched integration binaries `blind_floor` 7, `post_not_judged` 6, `cutting_data` 5, `edge_break_gate` 4, `commands_undo` 32, `dirty_flag` 2, `project_roundtrip` 69 - all pass.\n\nNot exercised: the full suite (the pre-existing wgpu race upstream), and the on-screen widgets themselves - their formatting functions are pinned instead.\n\nChangelog: errors, warnings and status notes ride the document's units - an inch document hears inches (saved notes and machine-limit messages stay mm, each its own issue).\n\nFixes #578\n",
